{"name":"Gen Z Yellow","hex":"#f4e386","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["Former ISO 639-3 language code for Geman Deng."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Information.","Information about the location of a bird."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gen"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Generation Z","blocks":[{"text":"Generation Z, often shortened to Gen Z and informally known as Zoomers, is the demographic cohort succeeding Millennials and preceding Generation Alpha. Researchers and popular media use the mid-to-late 1990s as starting birth years and the early 2010s as ending birth years, with the generation typically being defined as people born from 1997 to 2012. Most members of Generation Z are the children of younger Baby Boomers, Generation X and older Millennials, and it is predicted that many will be the parents of members of younger Generation Alpha and Generation Beta."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Generation_timeline_simple.svg/330px-Generation_timeline_simple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generation_Z","wikidata":"Q1987589"},{"title":"Z","blocks":[{"text":"Z is the twenty-sixth and last letter of the Latin alphabet. It is used in the modern English alphabet, in the alphabets of other Western European languages, and in others worldwide. Its usual names in English are zed, which is most commonly used in British English, and zee, most commonly used in American English, with an occasional archaic variant izzard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Latin_letter_Z.svg/330px-Latin_letter_Z.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Z","wikidata":"Q9751"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Young_People_Net_Happiness_2016.png/500px-Young_People_Net_Happiness_2016.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Young_People_Net_Happiness_2016.png/500px-Young_People_Net_Happiness_2016.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoung_People_Net_Happiness_2016.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg/500px-LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg/1280px-LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg/500px-LongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Generation Z comes of age during the Information Age, which has influenced not just their societies but also their lifestyle choices","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALongWavesThreeParadigms.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Hand_Embroidery_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/50/Hand_Embroidery_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Floral prints are enjoying a revival in the 2020s thanks to Generation Z.[96]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHand_Embroidery_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%E2%80%98LG_Q7_BTS_%EC%97%90%EB%94%94%EC%85%98%E2%80%99_%EC%98%88%EC%95%BD_%ED%8C%90%EB%A7%A4_%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%91_%2842773472410%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-%E2%80%98LG_Q7_BTS_%EC%97%90%EB%94%94%EC%85%98%E2%80%99_%EC%98%88%EC%95%BD_%ED%8C%90%EB%A7%A4_%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%91_%2842773472410%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/%E2%80%98LG_Q7_BTS_%EC%97%90%EB%94%94%EC%85%98%E2%80%99_%EC%98%88%EC%95%BD_%ED%8C%90%EB%A7%A4_%EC%8B%9C%EC%9E%91_%2842773472410